Subject: SNP and CNV probe loci
Message-ID: <Hu3xNxaCx9M.8k8GzZqVgEgJ@aroma-affymetrix.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/aroma-affymetrix/c/Hu3xNxaCx9M/m/8k8GzZqVgEgJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am using aroma.affymetrix for pre-processing of data for CNV analysis.  Briefly, I normalize and estimate copy number with CRMAv2.  I use the calculated copy number along with the chromosomal locations from the ugp file to run CBS using segment from the DNAcopy package.  Then I analyze the segmented copy number calls with downstream software like RAE from MSKCC.

I am analyzing data collected on the GWS6 platform.  I am getting errors when multiple probes map to the same genomic location.  For example, probe SNP_A-8462292 and probe CN_1173216 both map to chromosome 6 locus 29837188.  Is this behavior expected?  Is there a work around for this issue?

Thanks,
Mike

